      "content": "thanks. but wait, can we be a bit more direct about it? i'm worried if we mention the \"0.06\" or say it's \"just below the threshold,\" the board might get hung up on the technicality and think the study failed. \n\nis there a way to write this where we don't actually use that phrase \"just below the threshold\" but still make it sound like we've got definitive proof that it works? something that just conveys the success without the technical baggage?",
